# # gnss_vel.py
#
# Process Level-1 GNSS positions into Level-2 displacement and velocity time series,
# from EITHER of two input types:
#
# - `track` : TRACK/GEOD Level-1 parquet file (generated by `export_level1.py`).
# - `ppp`   : NRCan CSRS-PPP daily `.csv` + `.pos` files.
#
# Only data ingestion and filtering differ between the two input types. All other
# steps are shared: local NEU, rotation, pole corrections, exclusions, 
# regularisation, Gaussian smoothing, velocities, export, plots.
#
# Supersedes `gnss_disp_vel.py` (TRACK) and `gnss_ppp_vel.py` (PPP).
#
# ## USAGE
#
#     python gnss_vel.py -h
#
# Or as a Notebook (JupyterLab: right-click -> Open With -> Notebook), putting
# arguments in the 'Running in a Notebook?' cell.
#
# ## DATA INPUTS
#
# Level-1 inputs are looked for in `$GNSS_L1DIR/<site>/`:
# - track: one file matching `pp.REGEX_L1_FILE` (`<site>_YYYY_DOY_YYYY_DOY_geod.parquet`)
# - ppp: `<year>/*.csv` and `<year>/*.pos` (one sub-directory per year). Use -ppp_glob to change.
#
# With `-input auto` (default), the parquet is used if present, otherwise PPP files.
#
# Options files, looked for in `$GNSS_L2DIR/<site>/` (or -optspath):
# - `origin_<site>.csv` : mandatory for track. For ppp, if absent, the origin is
#   the mean of the first 100 epochs that pass the PPP filters (not saved).
# - `rotation_<site>.dat` : created if absent. For track, from all Level-1 epochs;
#   for ppp, from the epochs that pass the PPP filters.
# - `exclusions_<site>.csv`, `pole_corrections_<site>.csv` : optional.
#
# Filter parameters (YAML):
# - Default: `level2_parameter_defaults.yaml` (track) or `level2_parameter_defaults_ppp.yaml` (ppp),
#   both in the package directory. Override with -f.
# - Temporal adjustments: -tf. Supported keys: track -> filter_positions_episodic,
#   filter_positions_continuous, remove_displacement_outliers; ppp -> filter_positions_ppp.
#
# ## OUTPUTS (in `$GNSS_L2DIR/<site>/`)
# - `<site>_YYYY_DOY_YYYY_DOY_disp[_PPP].h5`, velocity CSVs, filter-parameters YAML, plots.
#   PPP outputs carry a `_PPP` suffix so they never overwrite TRACK outputs of the same period.
#
# ## HISTORY
# - Based on `plot_site_rel_2009_2012_geod.m` (Matt King, Andrew Sole, Ian Bartholomew, Andrew Tedstone, 2009-2012).
# - `gnss_disp_vel.py` created 2022-07-27 AJT, various updates to Sep 2026 - most important:
# - New epoch-by-epoch velocities calculations, Nov. 2025, AJT.
# - Moved filter parameters to YAML files, Dec. 2025, AJT.
# - Added new average-based processing for short daily observation blocks, Sep. 2026, AJT.
# - `gnss_ppp_vel.py` created August 2026 AJT.
# - Merged into `gnss_vel.py`, Sep. 2026.
#

